form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Clause + けれども","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"行きたいけれども時間がありません。","romaji":"Ikitai keredomo jikan ga arimasen.","meaning":"I want to go, but I do not have time."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Clause + けれども as shown in Clause + けれども."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-20-meaning","prompt":"What does “Clause + けれども” mean?","options":["But / although","Must / have to","Have to","Do not have to"],"answer":"But / although","explanation":"Clause + けれども expresses but / although. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-20-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “But けれども”.","options":["ない-form without い + なければならない","ない-form without い + なくてはいけない","ない-form + といけない","Clause + けれども"],"answer":"Clause + けれども","explanation":"Clause + けれども expresses but / although. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-20-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “But けれども”?","options":["宿題をしなくてはいけません。","もう帰らないといけません。","行きたいけれども時間がありません。","毎日薬を飲まなければなりません。"],"answer":"行きたいけれども時間がありません。","explanation":"行きたいけれども時間がありません。 (Ikitai keredomo jikan ga arimasen.) means “I want to go, but I do not have time.”."},{"id":"n4-20-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 行きたいけれども時間がありません。","options":["I have to go home now.","I want to go, but I do not have time.","I must take medicine every day.","I have to do my homework."],"answer":"I want to go, but I do not have time.","explanation":"行きたいけれども時間がありません。 (Ikitai keredomo jikan ga arimasen.) means “I want to go, but I do not have time.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":21,"category":"Contrast","title":"But / background が","pattern":"Clause + が + clause","meaning":"But / although","explanation":"Clause + が + clause expresses but / although. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Clause + が + clause","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。","romaji":"Kono hon wa muzukashii desu ga omoshiroi desu.","meaning":"This book is difficult but interesting."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Clause + が + clause as shown in Clause + が + clause."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-21-meaning","prompt":"What does “Clause + が + clause” mean?","options":["Must / have to","Have to","Do not have to","But / although"],"answer":"But / although","explanation":"Clause + が + clause expresses but / although. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-21-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “But / background が”.","options":["ない-form without い + なくてはいけない","ない-form + といけない","Clause + が + clause","ない-form without い + なければならない"],"answer":"Clause + が + clause","explanation":"Clause + が + clause expresses but / although. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-21-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “But / background が”?","options":["もう帰らないといけません。","この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。","毎日薬を飲まなければなりません。","宿題をしなくてはいけません。"],"answer":"この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。","explanation":"この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。 (Kono hon wa muzukashii desu ga omoshiroi desu.) means “This book is difficult but interesting.”."},{"id":"n4-21-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。","options":["This book is difficult but interesting.","I must take medicine every day.","I have to do my homework.","I have to go home now."],"answer":"This book is difficult but interesting.","explanation":"この本は難しいですがおもしろいです。 (Kono hon wa muzukashii desu ga omoshiroi desu.) means “This book is difficult but interesting.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":22,"category":"Reasons","title":"Multiple reasons し","pattern":"Clause + し + clause + し","meaning":"Both ... and / reasons","explanation":"Clause + し + clause + し expresses both ... and / reasons. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Plain clause + し + plain clause + し","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。","romaji":"Kono machi wa shizuka da shi benri da shi sumiyasui desu.","meaning":"This town is quiet and convenient, so it is easy to live in."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Clause + し + clause + し as shown in Plain clause + し + plain clause + し."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-22-meaning","prompt":"What does “Clause + し + clause + し” mean?","options":["Have to","Do not have to","Both ... and / reasons","Must / have to"],"answer":"Both ... and / reasons","explanation":"Clause + し + clause + し expresses both ... and / reasons. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-22-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Multiple reasons し”.","options":["ない-form + といけない","Plain clause + し + plain clause + し","ない-form without い + なければならない","ない-form without い + なくてはいけない"],"answer":"Plain clause + し + plain clause + し","explanation":"Clause + し + clause + し expresses both ... and / reasons. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-22-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Multiple reasons し”?","options":["この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。","毎日薬を飲まなければなりません。","宿題をしなくてはいけません。","もう帰らないといけません。"],"answer":"この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。","explanation":"この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。 (Kono machi wa shizuka da shi benri da shi sumiyasui desu.) means “This town is quiet and convenient, so it is easy to live in.”."},{"id":"n4-22-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。","options":["I must take medicine every day.","I have to do my homework.","I have to go home now.","This town is quiet and convenient, so it is easy to live in."],"answer":"This town is quiet and convenient, so it is easy to live in.","explanation":"この町は静かだし便利だし住みやすいです。 (Kono machi wa shizuka da shi benri da shi sumiyasui desu.) means “This town is quiet and convenient, so it is easy to live in.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":23,"category":"Examples","title":"Representative actions たり","pattern":"Verb た-form + り + する","meaning":"Do things such as","explanation":"Verb た-form + り + する expresses do things such as. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Verb た-form + り + verb た-form + り + する","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"週末は映画を見たり買い物をしたりします。","romaji":"Shuumatsu wa eiga o mitari kaimono o shitari shimasu.","meaning":"On weekends I do things such as watch movies and shop."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Verb た-form + り + する as shown in Verb た-form + り + verb た-form + り + する."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-23-meaning","pr