home now.","You should not drink coffee late at night.","I must take medicine every day."],"answer":"You should not drink coffee late at night.","explanation":"夜遅くコーヒーを飲まないほうがいいです。 (Yoru osoku koohii o nomanai hou ga ii desu.) means “You should not drink coffee late at night.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":44,"category":"Advice","title":"Ought to べき","pattern":"Verb dictionary + べきだ","meaning":"Ought to","explanation":"Verb dictionary + べきだ expresses ought to. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Verb dictionary + べきだ","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"約束は守るべきです。","romaji":"Yakusoku wa mamoru beki desu.","meaning":"You should keep your promises."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Verb dictionary + べきだ as shown in Verb dictionary + べきだ."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-44-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb dictionary + べきだ” mean?","options":["Ought to","Must / have to","Have to","Do not have to"],"answer":"Ought to","explanation":"Verb dictionary + べきだ expresses ought to. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-44-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Ought to べき”.","options":["ない-form without い + なければならない","ない-form without い + なくてはいけない","ない-form + といけない","Verb dictionary + べきだ"],"answer":"Verb dictionary + べきだ","explanation":"Verb dictionary + べきだ expresses ought to. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-44-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Ought to べき”?","options":["宿