ve る + れば","explanation":"Verb ば-form expresses if / provided that. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-45-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “If ば”?","options":["このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。","時間があれば映画を見ます。","家に帰ったら電話してください。","日本へ行くなら春がいいです。"],"answer":"時間があれば映画を見ます。","explanation":"時間があれば映画を見ます。 (Jikan ga areba eiga o mimasu.) means “If I have time, I will watch a movie.”."},{"id":"n4-45-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 時間があれば映画を見ます。","options":["If I have time, I will watch a movie.","When you get home, please call me.","If you are going to Japan, spring is good.","When you press this button, the door opens."],"answer":"If I have time, I will watch a movie.","explanation":"時間があれば映画を見ます。 (Jikan ga areba eiga o mimasu.) means “If I have time, I will watch a movie.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":46,"category":"Condition","title":"If / when たら","pattern":"Verb た-form + ら","meaning":"If / when","explanation":"Verb た-form + ら expresses if / when. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Verb た-form + ら","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"家に帰ったら電話してください。","romaji":"Ie ni kaettara denwa shite kudasai.","meaning":"When you get home, please call me."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Verb た-form + ら as shown in Verb た-form + ら."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-46-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb た-form + ら” mean?","options":["If that is the case","When / whenever (natural result)","If / when","If / provided that"],"answer":"If / when","explanation":"Verb た-form + ら expresses if / when. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-46-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “If / when たら”.","options":["Verb dictionary + と","Verb た-form + ら","Group 1 e-row + ば; Group 2 remove る + れば","Noun / plain clause + なら"],"answer":"Verb た-form + ら","explanation":"Verb た-form + ら expresses if / when. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-46-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “If / when たら”?","options":["家に帰ったら電話してください。","時間があれば映画を見ます。","日本へ行くなら春がいいです。","このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。"],"answer":"家に帰ったら電話してください。","explanation":"家に帰ったら電話してください。 (Ie ni kaettara denwa shite kudasai.) means “When you get home, please call me.”."},{"id":"n4-46-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 家に帰ったら電話してください。","options":["If I have time, I will watch a movie.","If you are going to Japan, spring is good.","When you press this button, the door opens.","When you get home, please call me."],"answer":"When you get home, please call me.","explanation":"家に帰ったら電話してください。 (Ie ni kaettara denwa shite kudasai.) means “When you get home, please call me.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":47,"category":"Condition","title":"If that is the case なら","pattern":"Noun / plain clause + なら","meaning":"If that is the case","explanation":"Noun / plain clause + なら expresses if that is the case. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Noun / plain clause + なら","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"日本へ行くなら春がいいです。","romaji":"Nihon e iku nara haru ga ii desu.","meaning":"If you are going to Japan, spring is good."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Noun / plain clause + なら as shown in Noun / plain clause + なら."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-47-meaning","prompt":"What does “Noun / plain clause + なら” mean?","options":["When / whenever (natural result)","If that is the case","If / provided that","If / when"],"answer":"If that is the case","explanation":"Noun / plain clause + なら expresses if that is the case. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-47-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “If that is the case なら”.","options":["Noun / plain clause + なら","Group 1 e-row + ば; Group 2 remove る + れば","Verb た-form + ら","Verb dictionary + と"],"answer":"Noun / plain clause + なら","explanation":"Noun / plain clause + なら expresses if that is the case. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-47-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “If that is the case なら”?","options":["時間があれば映画を見ます。","家に帰ったら電話してください。","このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。","日本へ行くなら春がいいです。"],"answer":"日本へ行くなら春がいいです。","explanation":"日本へ行くなら春がいいです。 (Nihon e iku nara haru ga ii desu.) means “If you are going to Japan, spring is good.”."},{"id":"n4-47-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 日本へ行くなら春がいいです。","options":["When you get home, please call me.","When you press this button, the door opens.","If you are going to Japan, spring is good.","If I have time, I will watch a movie."],"answer":"If you are going to Japan, spring is good.","explanation":"日本へ行くなら春がいいです。 (Nihon e iku nara haru ga ii desu.) means “If you are going to Japan, spring is good.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":48,"category":"Condition","title":"Natural result と","pattern":"Verb dictionary + と","meaning":"When / whenever (natural result)","explanation":"Verb dictionary + と expresses when / whenever (natural result). Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Verb dictionary + と","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。","romaji":"Kono botan o osu to doa ga akimasu.","meaning":"When you press this button, the door opens."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Verb dictionary + と as shown in Verb dictionary + と."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-48-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb dictionary + と” mean?","options":["When / whenever (natural result)","If / provided that","If / when","If that is the case"],"answer":"When / whenever (natural result)","explanation":"Verb dictionary + と expresses when / whenever (natural result). Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-48-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Natural result と”.","options":["Group 1 e-row + ば; Group 2 remove る + れば","Verb た-form + ら","Noun / plain clause + なら","Verb dictionary + と"],"answer":"Verb dictionary + と","explanation":"Verb dictionary + と expresses when / whenever (natural result). Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-48-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Natural result と”?","options":["家に帰ったら電話してください。","日本へ行くなら春がいいです。","このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。","時間があれば映画を見ます。"],"answer":"このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。","explanation":"このボタンを押すとドアが開きます。 (Kono botan o osu to doa ga akimasu.) means “When you press this button, the door opens.”."},{"id":"n4-48-tran