required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-49-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Even if ても”?","options":["もう帰らないといけません。","雨が降っても行きます。","毎日薬を飲まなければなりません。","宿題をしなくてはいけません。"],"answer":"雨が降っても行きます。","explanation":"雨が降っても行きます。 (Ame ga futte mo ikimasu.) means “Even if it rains, I will go.”."},{"id":"n4-49-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 雨が降っても行きます。","options":["Even if it rains, I will go.","I must take medicine every day.","I have to do my homework.","I have to go home now."],"answer":"Even if it rains, I will go.","explanation":"雨が降っても行きます。 (Ame ga futte mo ikimasu.) means “Even if it rains, I will go.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N4","sort_order":50,"category":"Situation","title":"In the case 場合","pattern":"Verb plain / noun の + 場合","meaning":"In the case of","explanation":"Verb plain / noun の + 場合 expresses in the case of. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern.","formation":"Plain form + 場合; noun + の場合","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"雨の場合試合は中止です。","romaji":"Ame no baai shiai wa chuushi desu.","meaning":"In case of rain, the match is cancelled."}],"common_mistakes":["Do not substitute a nearby expression with a different nuance. Build the verb or clause first, then attach Verb plain / noun の + 場合 as shown in Plain form + 場合; noun + の場合."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n4-50-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb plain / noun の + 場合” mean?","options":["Have to","Do not have to","In the case of","Must / have to"],"answer":"In the case of","explanation":"Verb plain / noun の + 場合 expresses in the case of. Use this construction to connect the stated action, condition or viewpoint to the rest of the sentence. Check the required plain, て, た or negative form before adding the pattern."},{"id":"n4-50-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “In the case 場合”.","